Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14050792/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-105162" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\pi \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi t+t"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14050792/state.json" "file_sha256" "72a4f4389fa4f7d9bc02cd66c0bff65dfb2b3294a95e880f7f48fe02286dbca5" "basis" 1760 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14050792/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-105162" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "t\\pi \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi t"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14050792/state.json" "file_sha256" "72a4f4389fa4f7d9bc02cd66c0bff65dfb2b3294a95e880f7f48fe02286dbca5" "basis" 1760 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14050792/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-105162" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3t"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14050792/state.json" "file_sha256" "72a4f4389fa4f7d9bc02cd66c0bff65dfb2b3294a95e880f7f48fe02286dbca5" "basis" 1760 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14050792/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-98750" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $V=C[0,1],$ the vector space of functions that are continuous over $[0,1].$ Given that the inner product on $V$ is defined as \n\n$$\n⟨x(t),y(t)⟩={\\int }_{0}^{1}x(t)y(t)\\,\\text{d}t,\n$$\n\nfind the distance between $f(t)=2t$ and the subspace spanned by $g(t)=6t-3$ with respect to the inner product." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14050792/state.json" "file_sha256" "72a4f4389fa4f7d9bc02cd66c0bff65dfb2b3294a95e880f7f48fe02286dbca5" "basis" 1760 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14050792/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-98750" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The orthogonal projection of $f(t)$ onto $\\text{Span}{g(t)}$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{g(t)}\\,f(t) & =\\frac{⟨f(t),g(t)⟩}{⟨g(t),g(t)⟩}\\,g(t) \\\\  & =\\frac{{\\int }_{0}^{1}2t\\cdot (6t-3)\\,\\text{d}t}{{\\int }_{0}^{1}(6t-3)^{2}\\,\\text{d}t}\\cdot (6t-3) \\\\  & =\\frac{{\\int }_{0}^{1}(12{t}^{2}-6t)\\,\\text{d}t}{{\\int }_{0}^{1}(36{t}^{2}-36t+9)\\,\\text{d}t}\\cdot (6t-3) \\\\  & =\\frac{{[4{t}^{3}-3{t}^{2}]}_{0}^{1}}{{[12{t}^{3}-18{t}^{2}+9t]}_{0}^{1}}\\cdot (6t-3) \\\\  & =\\frac{(4-3)-0}{(12-18+9)-0}\\cdot (6t-3) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot (6t-3) \\\\  & =2t-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe distance between $f(t)=2t$ and the subspace spanned by $g(t)=6t-3$ with respect to our inner product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =‖f(t)-{\\text{proj}}_{g(t)}\\,f(t)‖ \\\\  & =‖2t-(2t-1)‖ \\\\  & =‖1‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{⟨1,1⟩}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the inner product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨1,1⟩ & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}1\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =t{|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =1-0 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the distance is $d=\\sqrt{1}=1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14050792/state.json" "file_sha256" "72a4f4389fa4f7d9bc02cd66c0bff65dfb2b3294a95e880f7f48fe02286dbca5" "basis" 1760 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/math